.Dd September 21, 2026
.Dt SLICE 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm slice
.Nd extract a specific segment of bytes from input
.
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl f Ar from
.Op Fl t Ar to
.Op Ar --
.Op Ar input
.
.Nm
.Op Fl f Ar from
.Op Fl l Ar length
.Op Ar --
.Op Ar input
.
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.ad l
.Nm
extracts a subsection of
.Ar input
beginning at the byte offset specified by
.Fl -from ,
and ending at the offset specified by either
.Fl -to
or
.Fl -length .
If neither
.Fl -to
nor
.Fl -length
are specified,
.Nm
reads
.Ar input
from its starting point until completion.
If
.Ar input
is omitted or set to the string
.Ql - ,
.Nm
reads from standard input.
.Bl -tag -width 4n
.It Fl f , -from Ar offset
Specify the beginning of the byte-range to read,
measured from the beginning of the input stream.
If omitted,
.Nm
will begin reading from the start of input as though
.Ql Fl -from Sy 0
were used.
.It Fl h , -help
Print a terse usage message to standard output,
then exit.
.It Fl l , -length Ar bytes
Specify the size of the byte-range to read,
measured from the offset set by
.Fl -from ,
or the start of the input stream if the latter is unspecified.
This option is incompatible with
.Fl -to .
.It Fl t , -to Ar offset
Specify the end of the byte-range to read,
measured from the beginning of the input stream.
If omitted,
.Nm
will continue reading until EOF is reached.
This option is incompatible with
.Fl -length .
.El
.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width 4n
.It Ev DD_EXEC
Command to use instead of the
.Xr dd 1
version found in the user's
.Ev PATH .
.El
.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Pull a 2.5 MBs file from an unmounted volume:
.Dl Nm Fl f Ar 129252200448 Fl l Ar 2621440 Ar /dev/rdisk2
.Pp
Print the contents of a file without the initial 500-byte header:
.Dl Nm Fl f Ar 500 Ar input.c
.
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
.Bl -ohang
.It Sy Option \(aq Ns No ... Ns Sy \(aq missing argument
The invocation of
.Nm
ended with a switch that anticipated an argument.
.It Sy Invalid byte offset:
A non-numeric or empty value was given where a byte-offset was expected,
or the offset was a negative or non-integral value.
.It Sy Cannot slice directory object
.Nm Ap s Ar input
argument pointed to a directory object,
instead of a regular file,
FIFO,
or device special file.
.It Sy Options Fl -to Sy and Fl -length Sy are mutually exclusive
The endpoint of the range to be read is ambiguous due to conflicting parameters.
.It Sy End offset must be greater than starting offset
The value of the
.Fl -to
option is equal to or less than the value of
.Fl -from .
.It Sy Length argument must be greater than zero
The value of the
.Fl -length
option is either zero or a negative value.
.El
.
