.Sh CAVEATS
The
.Nm
command is
.Em not
written to be performant.
Its code is optimised for accuracy and portability,
and thus takes into consideration the various limitations of different
.Xr dd 1
flavours.
It also endeavours to be compatible with as many POSIX-compliant shells;
however,
.Xr posh 1
.Pq at least as of version 0.14.1 on macOS
proved too buggy to accommodate.
.
.Sh BUGS
Offsets specified on the command-line do not support unit multipliers.
.Pp
A
.Dq Fl -write Ns No = Ns Ar string
option to overwrite specified byte-ranges ought to be added.
